set.body:
Complete the lifecycle outside OperatorProgram.

Pipeline:
Study -> fitted preprocessing/alignment -> estimated operator diagram -> certified operator policies -> OperatorProgram -> lowered solve -> certified fit -> transform new observations.

ModelSpec owns:
- centering/scaling and missingness policies;
- learned alignments, charts, graphs, and statistical estimators;
- shrinkage and regularization selection;
- solver policy and capabilities;
- nested/cross-validation orchestration;
- fitted transformations and provenance.

Acceptance:
- leakage tests prove every data-dependent operation is fit only on training folds;
- deterministic seeds and split identities are recorded;
- transform rejects incompatible nominal spaces and feature identities;
- nested tuning fixtures compare against a hand-executed reference pipeline;
- requested/lowered programs, active terms/constraints, effective operators, auxiliary variables, guarantees, and full provenance are inspectable;
- focused JVM/JS tests plus compileAll/testAll pass at one committed tip.
